--- double-double p=3 e=-1..2  (radix 2, 982 values)
    note: i1's generator produced the plain float here
    verdict            : OUTSIDE: a binade is not an arithmetic progression
    binades            : 5 (0 hold one value and pin no step)

--- logarithmic number system, base 2, three fraction bits
    2^(k/8) for k = 1..64, rational at all: 8 of 64
    verdict            : OUTSIDE: values are not m * r^q

SUMMARY over 21 value sets plus the logarithmic case:
  inside the affine-grid-per-binade concept : 18 of 21
    of those, at bias zero (Flocq generic_format): 17
    of those, needing a nonzero bias            : 1
    FIXED: 10
    FLOAT: 2
    FLOAT with gradual underflow: 3
    SEGMENTED: 3
  outside, with the clause that fails:
    decimal p=2 e=-2..2 at radix 2: OUTSIDE: values are not m * r^q
    fixed-slash P=7 Q=7: OUTSIDE: values are not m * r^q
    double-double p=3 e=-1..2: OUTSIDE: a binade is not an arithmetic progression
    logarithmic number system: OUTSIDE: values are not m * r^q
